>## Construct an OrderingIsomorphism between two orderings of the same elements. The two list arguments must be permutations of each other; the result is a pair of mappings that transport an element list from one ordering to the other.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>term createOrderingIsomorphism = λsourceOrd,targetOrd.let sourceToTargetMapping := λels.let mp := maps.fromList (lists.zip sourceOrd els) in optionals.givens (lists.map (λn.maps.lookup n mp) targetOrd) in let targetToSourceMapping := λels.let mp := maps.fromList (lists.zip targetOrd els) in optionals.givens (lists.map (λn.maps.lookup n mp) sourceOrd) in topology.OrderingIsomorphism{encode = sourceToTargetMapping, decode = targetToSourceMapping}
