>## Sort a directed acyclic graph (DAG) of nodes using two helper functions: one for node keys, and one for the adjacency list of connected node keys. The result is a list of strongly-connected components (cycles), in which singleton lists represent acyclic nodes.
#^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
#  ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ source.hydra comment.block.documentation.hydra
>term topologicalSortNodes = λgetKey,getAdj,nodes.let nodesByKey := maps.fromList (lists.map (λn.(getKey n, n)) nodes) in let pairs := lists.map (λn.(getKey n, getAdj n)) nodes in let comps := topologicalSortComponents pairs in lists.map (λc.optionals.givens (lists.map (λk.maps.lookup k nodesByKey) c)) comps
